From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:43:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: deliver signals for exceptions (SIGSEGV, ...),
 sigaltstack

The kernel calls a registered exception handler on a synchronous
exception in user mode; on aarch64 relibc registered none, so a bad
memory access ended the process without a signal.

- __relibc_internal_excpentry: same frame as the signal entry, switches
  to the sigaltstack if the signal has SA_ONSTACK, runs inner_excp and
  returns through the signal entry's restore part.
- map_err_code and the SA_ONSTACK bitset per exception class (ESR_EL1.EC).
- The signal entry switches to the sigaltstack with SA_ONSTACK, and
  arch_pre reports it in uc_stack.
- Like the signal entry since relibc 0013 (redox-rpi #127), inner_excp
  writes pc and x0 to the sigcontrol struct and sets SIGRETURN_UNINHIBIT,
  and the exception entry returns through `svc #0x5352`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 redox-rt/src/arch/aarch64.rs | 178 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 redox-rt/src/signal.rs       |  53 ++++++++---
 2 files changed, 203 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

